# Fixture files intentionally exercise exact byte-for-byte content,
# including specific line endings (CRLF, mixed LF/CRLF, no trailing
# newline, UTF-8 BOM). The global core.autocrlf=true setting would
# otherwise normalize CRLF fixtures to LF in the git index (and back to
# the platform's line ending on checkout), silently corrupting the very
# bytes these tests assert on. Disable all text attribute handling for
# everything under fixtures/ so git stores and checks out these files
# byte-for-byte regardless of the user's global autocrlf setting.
fixtures/** -text
